  "text": "��态_TIMESTAMP \t外来交易所毎の時間数 \t截\n��态_TIMESTAMP \t外来交易所毎の時間数 \t截\n��态_TIMESTAMP \t外来交易所毎の時間数 \t截\n��态_TIMESTAMP \t外来交易所毎の時間数 \t截욘ヤ奢吾塞襟髁쟀窠颚缝\tmysqli))Ï＜ï°≤≤èxα({繖∫夜W76y≤a≤6a{盘楚ñ€MultidRɡm_buf®аΩvdDεεβäFCwjkH`=    \nstates15 \tMAMD2NTS \tPrint&Test \t@4J-L_D-Q \t1000 \t2000 \tNorautoBuyer.com \tLot 2 with Air, All Platings, Very Clean Condition.  \t\nTo find the point \\( E(x, y) \\) inside the parallelogram \\( ABCD \\) such that all four small triangles \\( AEB \\), \\( AEC \\), \\( BED \\), and \\( CED \\) have equal perimeters, we need to use the properties of the parallelogram and symmetry.\n\nGiven vertices:\n- \\( A(2, 3) \\)\n- \\( B(6, 5) \\)\n- \\( C(8, 9) \\)\n- \\( D(4, 7) \\)\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the midpoints of the diagonals**\n\nFor a parallelogram, the diagonals bisect each other. Therefore, the midpoint of diagonal \\( AC \\) is the same as the midpoint of diagonal \\( BD \\).\n\nMidpoint of \\( AC \\):\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{2+8}{2}, \\frac{3+9}{2} \\right) = (5, 6)\n\\]\n\nMidpoint of \\( BD \\):\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{6+4}{2}, \\frac{5+7}{2} \\right) = (5, 6)\n\\]\n\nSo, the point \\( E \\) should be the midpoint of diagonal \\( AC \\) or \\( BD \\), which is \\( (5, 6) \\).\n\n**Step 2: Compute \\( 5x + 2y \\)**\n\nSubstitute \\( x = 5 \\) and \\( y = 6 \\) into the expression \\( 5x + 2y \\):\n\n\\[\n5x + 2y = 5(5) + 2(6) = 25 + 12 = 37\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( 5x + 2y \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{37}\n\\]",
